# EN / AR and RTL

The site is bilingual. Locale key: `localStorage['rate-me-locale']` = `en` | `ar`. Arabic uses Noto Sans Arabic and `.arabic-mode`.

## Rules

- Every user-visible string needs an Arabic equivalent. Update `arabicCopy` (or a future dictionary) in the same change.
- Set `document.documentElement.lang` and `dir` (`ltr` / `rtl`) together.
- Use `data-rate-me-copy` when text is not a plain text node (buttons with icons).
- Do not machine-translate legal, pricing, or the score formula. Keep **Rayt Me** untranslated as the product name.
- Layout must work in RTL: logical properties (`ps`/`pe`, `ms`/`me`) over `left`/`right` for new CSS. Mirror illustrations via `.arabic-mode` when needed.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — English-only control
<button>Get started</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button><span data-rate-me-copy>Get started</span></button>
// arabicCopy['Get started'] === 'ابدأ الآن'
```

## Copy discipline

Translate meaning, not word-for-word. Keep professional register in Arabic. FAQ answers must stay consistent with product truth (evidence, disputes, privacy).
